    "### 2.3. Part-of-Speech Tagging\n",
    "\n",
    "Does the grammatical role of the first word influence title performance? Titles starting with action verbs (imperative, e.g., \"Kill a Mockingbird\", \"Find Me\") may convey urgency and drive higher engagement compared to titles starting with nouns (e.g., \"The Hunger Games\", \"Harry Potter\")."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "526a90a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "PART-OF-SPEECH ANALYSIS: Starting Word Performance\n",
      "================================================================================\n",
      "\n",
      "📊 Performance by Starting Word's Part-of-Speech:\n",
      "                       Total_Checkouts  Avg_Checkouts  Title_Count  \\\n",
      "starting_pos_category                                                \n",
